SYNTHESIS
  1. In the HYP-2694 quotient, the one-part block [m] is the exact
     decorrelated maximizer for every m=7..11; every split loses.
  2. The exact single-block cover is below cap_k with margin at least
     the k=9 margin shown above, about 0.18862.
  3. For actual shifted single blocks, the cell-freeze BV lemma gives
     a rigorous large-M closure once 7*binom(m,2)/M is below that margin.
  4. Remaining HYP-2694 work is the multi-block/multi-carrier version:
     prove the analogous joint decorrelation error is bounded by the
     available split gap plus cap margin, then finite-check the small gaps.
